From 110c22bed2ec4afc57bdfe249bd7b8e0233b02db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:28:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] drm/vc4: hdmi: Attach the "Dolby Vision" property

vc4 checks the HDMI connector state with the HDMI state helper and
writes the infoframes with it when the encoder is enabled, so it only
needs to attach the property. The Dolby vendor infoframe, 31 bytes with
its header, fits a packet RAM slot (VC4_HDMI_PACKET_SIZE).

Tested on a Raspberry Pi 5 with an LG B4 (webOS 9.1) at 3840x2160 24 Hz:
the TV reports Dolby Vision with either value, shows the tunnelled frames
correctly, and returns to SDR with Off.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
index e858a5b87..559825397 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
@@ -599,6 +599,10 @@ static int vc4_hdmi_connector_init(struct drm_device *dev,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	ret = drm_connector_attach_dolby_vision_property(connector);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	drm_connector_attach_encoder(connector, encoder);
 
 	return 0;
